# Sketchdraw End User License Agreement

Version 1.0, 20 November 2026

Copyright (c) 2026 Jeremy Teichmann (J-ARTS). All rights reserved.

This agreement is between you and the licensor about Sketchdraw. Read
it before you download, install, copy or use the software. If you do
not agree to it, do not use the software.

## 1. Definitions

**Software** means Sketchdraw: the desktop application, its installers,
the session relay, the source code, the documentation and all other
files of the repository <https://github.com/J-ARTS/de.sketchdraw.io>
and of its releases, in source and in built form, including updates.
Third-party components (section 8) are not part of the software in
this sense.

**Licensor** means Jeremy Teichmann (J-ARTS), the holder of the rights
in the software.

**You** means the person who uses the software and, if you use it for
an organisation, that organisation as well.

**Official sources** are the repository named above and its release
pages.

**Commercial product** means any software, service or other offering
that is sold, licensed, rented or provided for a fee, that is financed
by advertising, subscriptions or paid features, or that is otherwise
offered to third parties with the intention of earning money, whether
or not it actually earns money.

**Permission** means the prior written permission of the licensor
(section 6).

## 2. Acceptance

You accept this agreement by downloading, installing, copying or using
the software. You may only do these things under this agreement.

## 3. What you may do

The licensor grants you, free of charge, a worldwide, non-exclusive,
non-transferable right, which you may not sublicense, to do the
following for as long as you keep to this agreement:

1. **Use.** Obtain the software from the official sources, install it
   on any number of devices and use it, for private purposes and for
   the internal purposes of your organisation, including in the course
   of paid work. Copies made to install the software on the devices of
   your own organisation are part of this use.
2. **Your own content.** Everything you create with the software, such
   as diagrams, documents and exports, belongs to you. You may use it
   for any purpose, including commercially.
3. **Study and adapt for yourself.** Read the source code, build the
   software from it and change it for your own use as described in
   number 1. You may not pass on changed versions (section 4.3).
4. **Agent skills.** Install the agent skills that come with the
   software in your own agent tools and keep copies of them in
   repositories of your organisation that are not public.
5. **Contribute.** Create a copy of the repository on the platform
   that hosts it for the sole purpose of preparing and proposing
   changes to the software to the licensor.

## 4. What you may not do

Without permission you may not do any of the following, either
yourself or through others.

### 4.1 No sale

You may not sell, rent, lease or lend the software, license it for a
fee, or otherwise ask for or accept payment or another consideration
for the software or for access to it. This applies to the software
alone, as part of a bundle, preinstalled on a device and as a hosted
or managed service.

### 4.2 No use of the code in commercial products

You may not use, copy, adapt, translate into another programming
language or otherwise build on the source code of the software, or on
any part of it, in a commercial product. This applies to the code, the
user interface and its design system, the artwork and the
documentation, and it applies whether or not the part has been changed.

Reading and writing Sketchdraw's file formats in your own software, and
connecting your own software to Sketchdraw through its documented
interfaces, is not a use of the code in this sense.

### 4.3 No republication

You may not publish, distribute, mirror or otherwise make available to
third parties the software or any part of it, changed or unchanged, in
source or in built form. This includes uploading it to another
repository, a package registry, an app store, a download portal or a
file-sharing service, and offering it under another name.

You may always point others to the official sources.

### 4.4 Further restrictions

You may not:

1. remove, hide or change copyright notices, this agreement or the
   third-party notices in the software;
2. use the name "Sketchdraw", the logo or the name of the licensor for
   your own products or services, or in a way that suggests the
   licensor supports or endorses you;
3. grant others rights in the software, or transfer this agreement;
4. use the software to break the law or the rights of others.

## 5. Platform terms

Nothing in this agreement limits rights that the terms of the platform
hosting the repository give you directly, for example to view the
repository there and to create a copy of it on that platform. Such a
copy may not be used for anything that section 4 prohibits.

## 6. Permission

The licensor can allow what section 4 prohibits. Ask through the
repository (<https://github.com/J-ARTS/de.sketchdraw.io/issues>) or the
licensor's profile (<https://github.com/J-ARTS>). Permission is only
valid if the licensor gives it in writing (text form, for example an
e-mail or a signed document), for the specific use named in it. Silence
is not permission.

## 7. Contributions

If you propose changes to the software to the licensor, you keep your
rights in them. You grant the licensor a worldwide, perpetual,
irrevocable, non-exclusive, royalty-free right to use, change, publish
and distribute your contribution as part of the software and to
license it to others under this agreement or under other terms. You
confirm that you are entitled to grant this right.

## 8. Third-party components

The software contains and uses components of third parties, for
example libraries, fonts and icon sets. They remain under their own
licences, which are named in the section "Third-Party Notices" below,
in `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`, in `THIRD_PARTY_ICONS.md` and in the
packages themselves. This agreement does not limit the rights those
licences give you in these components, and it does not give you rights
in the names and trademarks of their owners.

## 9. Earlier versions

Versions of the software that the licensor published before the date
of this agreement were published under the PolyForm Noncommercial
License 1.0.0. For copies of those versions, that licence continues to
apply. This agreement applies to Sketchdraw 0.1.7 and all later
versions, and to every revision of the repository that contains this
file.

## 10. Ownership

The software is licensed, not sold. The licensor keeps all rights in
the software that this agreement does not expressly grant.

## 11. Updates and support

The licensor may change, update or stop offering the software at any
time and does not owe support, maintenance or updates. The desktop
application can ask the official sources whether a newer version
exists.

## 12. End of your rights

Your rights under this agreement end automatically if you do something
that section 4 prohibits. They also end if you break another term of
this agreement and do not put this right within 30 days after the
licensor has told you about it. When your rights end, you must stop
using the software and delete all copies of it. The licensor can
restore your rights in writing. Sections 7 and 10 and sections 13 to 15
continue to apply.

## 13. No warranty

The software is provided free of charge and as it is. As far as the
law allows, the licensor gives no warranty and makes no promise about
the software, in particular not that it is free of errors, fit for a
particular purpose, or that it does not lose data. You are responsible
for backups of your documents. The licensor is liable for defects only
if the licensor has fraudulently concealed them.

## 14. Liability

The licensor is liable without limit for intent and gross negligence,
for injury to life, body or health, and where the law does not allow
liability to be excluded, for example under product liability law. In
all other cases the licensor is not liable, as far as the law allows,
for any damage arising from the software or from its use, including
lost data, lost profit and interruption of business.

## 15. General terms

1. This agreement is governed by the law of the Federal Republic of
   Germany, without its conflict-of-law rules and without the United
   Nations Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods.
   If you are a consumer, the mandatory consumer protection rules of
   the country where you live continue to protect you.
2. If a term of this agreement is or becomes invalid, the other terms
   stay in force.
3. This agreement is the whole agreement between you and the licensor
   about the software. The licensor may publish new versions of this
   agreement for later versions of the software; a version of the
   software stays under the agreement it was published with.
4. This English text is the binding one. Translations and summaries
   are for convenience only.

